><surname>Kang</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kraft</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Gauderman</surname><given-names>WJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Thomas</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Multiple imputation methods for longitudinal blood pressure measurements from the Framingham Heart Study</article-title><source>BMC Genetics</source><year>2003</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>S43</fpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14975111</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1186/1471-2156-4-S1-S43</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><sec sec-type="display-objects"><title>Figures and Tables</title><fig position="float" id="F1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>QTL LOD scores for SBP residuals, chromosome 17.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="1471-2156-4-S1-S55-1"/></fig><table-wrap position="float" id="T1"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Univariate estimates of covariance parameters (and their standard errors) from the polygenic model</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><td align="left">Age interval</td><td align="center">Polygenic &#x003c3;<sub>a</sub><sup>2</sup></td><td align="center">Error &#x003c3;<sub>e</sub><sup>2</sup></td><td align="center"><italic>n</italic></td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left">&#x0003c; 35 years</td><td align="center">34.99 (7.59)</td><td align="center">95.13 (7.38)</td><td align="center">1277</td></tr><tr><td align="left">35&#x02013;50 years</td><td align="center">63.74 (7.45)</td><td align="center">128.13 (6.76)</td><td align="center">2411</td></tr><tr><td align="left">50&#x02013;65 years</td><td align="center">109.44 (14.76)</td><td align="center">214.57 (13.43)</td><td align="center">2030</td></tr><tr><td align="left">&#x0003e; 65 years</td><td align="center">317.36 (67.16)</td><td align="center">535.43 (63.14)</td><td align="center">1133</td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap position="float" id="T2"><l